PATCH 409: faithful 16-bit reconstruction of the MGAVIDEO transparency sprite blit FUN_0000_298a
(asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x298a-0x29f3), superseding patch 136's loop body.

THE BUG (wasm "memory access out of bounds"; native: silent memory corruption).  On the live mission
paint pass the wireframe unit blitter 294d->298a is handed a sprite record whose header width byte
(word[si-4] low) is 0 (asm-observed: recseg=5add recoff=20ca srch=1b00 => W=0 H=0x1b, at on-screen
dst di=rowtab[116]+107).  Patch 136 rebased the ES/rowtab/stride/source bases correctly but kept
Ghidra's model of the ES:DI dest cursor as a flat 32-bit host pointer and the row/col counters as
32-bit ints.  The asm inner `mov cx,dx ; loop` and outer `pop cx ; loop` are 16-bit: cx=W=0 makes
`loop` run 65536 times with the 16-bit DI wrapping exactly once through the 64KB VGA segment (harmless
in real mode).  Ghidra's 32-bit `uint` counter instead underflowed 0->0xffffffff and the flat dest
pointer marched out of g_mem -> wasm trap (native corrupts memory past 0xA0000 and limps on).  Confirmed
by catching the crashing call in the browser (-g2 build, stack 298a<-294d<-786b<-459a) and reading the
header W=0 at the trap; g_d298 debug scratch at linear 0x2011020 (just past g_mem+0x1000000) held the
blit's own spilled pixels -- the marker being overwritten IS the OOB dest march.

Same 16-bit-wrap class as patch 178 (2595 MASK fill) and patch 294 (23d8 cockpit-panel RLE): the
faithful fix is a direct transliteration with uint16_t di/si/cx, NOT an upstream W!=0 guard (per the
patch-294 oracle doctrine: the original reaches the blit with the edge-case record and survives via
segment wrap, so bit-identity requires we wrap too -- both di AND si, since the W=0 flat path reads
65536 source bytes and real-mode SI wraps in the DS segment).

  dst = ES:DI, ES=word[[0x724]][0], DI=rowtab[param_4]+param_2 (rowtab=[0x794])   -- di 16-bit, wraps
  stride bp = word[[0x724]+4] (xor/sub param_1 idiom, = itself for param_1=0)
  src = DS:SI, DS=m_260c_recseg (entry ES), SI=param_3 ; header word[si-4]: hi=H rows, lo=W cols
  flat path (29b6..29cc): per row, W bytes lods'd, each stos'd (nonzero) or skipped (di++); di-=W; di+=bp
  RLE path (29d2..29f0): per row, lods skip (di+=skip), lods count, count bytes stos/skip; di=rowstart+bp

Reached only on the in-mission 459a paint (wireframe unit blit); unreached by the verify flow matrix
-> native<->wasm byte-identity across the matrix is preserved.  Sources stay pristine; fist_mga.c via
build/.  board:0001

